INSERT INTO `dorm_static_info` VALUES ('47 Claremont','47 Claremont Avenue','47 Claremont Avenue, commonly known as Claremont, is located on Claremont Avenue, right off of 119th Street. The residence hall primarily houses sophomores and juniors in suites of three to seven people and has private bathrooms and kitchens. Claremont is beloved for its vicinity to Barnard facilities and buildings, including the Milstein Center for Teaching and Learning. Although it is slightly secluded from the main Columbia dining halls, Claremont residents say they get an intimate, tight-knit suite living experience and enjoy quick access to Riverside Park. ','Behind the scenes of campus','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/FHXBX6S53BANRLVYYEP2SM7KBQ.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Lots of storage space in rooms and in the kitchen#Very clean dorm, weekly cleanings#Close to Barnard and Riverside Park and a short walk to restaurants north of campus ','No AC#Some rooms have low light#Fire escape grates look like a jail cell#Only 1 bathroom per suite#Room size differences can be a little extreme; some places are cramped#A bit of hike to the 116th Street Columbia University subway station, mail room, and Butler Library ',40.810173,-73.963966,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',2,'0',NULL),('600 W 113th','600 West 113th Street','600 W. 113th St., located on 113th Street and Broadway, is the perfect place for you if you want to live in a large suite with your friends. The dorm is commonly known as Nuss due to its location above the restaurant Wu and Nussbaum. Nuss is just a block away from the main campus, but it also has close access to Community Food & Juice, Tom\'s Restaurant, Junzi Kitchen, Westside Market, and Duane Reade. The dorm is made up of apartment-style suites with a shared kitchen and private, semi-private, and shared bathrooms that vary by suite and floor. There is a mix of singles and doubles within suites. Nuss is quiet, cozy, convenient, and perfect for anyone who is looking for a more residential feel. ','A home with friends','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/52QDVVUAVJB6VPQ7HJZD77F2YY.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Flexible housing logistics (don\'t have to fill the suite)#Plenty of fridge and storage space in the kitchens#Building specific facilities desk: maintenance is not through Hartley Hospitality Desk (faster response time on most issues) ','Suites can be compact with narrow hallways#Common spaces are fairly small and crusty, with minimal furnishing ',40.806065,-73.965805,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors',1,'0','Nuss'),('Broadway Hall','114th Street and Broadway','Broadway Hall is a dorm located along 114th Street, and it consists of mainly singles and some doubles. The dorm houses a mix of sophomores, juniors, and seniors, with sophomores usually residing in doubles. It is fully air-conditioned and is a short walk not only from Lerner Hall and Ferris Booth Commons but also from Butler Library, John Jay Dining Hall, and JJ\'s Place. Broadway Hall contains a fitness room on the fourth floor and a sky lounge that features a study lounge, a reservable lounge, and a kitchen on each floor. There are also four music practice rooms. Many of the doubles, especially on the higher levels near the corners, have great views of the city, but the dorms in the center are shafted, so beware!','A hop and skip from campus','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/J7HNPO2AVRAC3HNWNHEMEMWOGM.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Sky lounge is very spacious, good for hanging out#Close to restaurants around Broadway, along with Ferris#Lots of amenities like practice rooms, gym, bike storage, and AC throughout the building ','Fitness room has no windows, can be suffocating#Rooms can be a little small, and walls are thin#Shafted dorms get little to no light, especially in the winter ',40.806091,-73.964722,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors',0,'0',NULL),('Carlton Arms','362 Riverside Drive','Carlton Arms is located on Riverside Drive between 108th and 109th Street. It is the farthest Columbia dorm from main campus, but many still choose it because of its large suites consisting of anywhere from four to 10 rooms (and maybe also because it was the only option left). If the distance seems like a great feat, know that if your room faces west, you can watch beautiful sunsets over the Hudson River every night. Students also report that the distance from campus can be a blessing in disguise, helping them feel more immersed in the liveliness of the Upper West Side. Beware that you\'ll have to brace yourself for the long walks and the first month of no air conditioning, but Carlton Arms is a primary option for sophomore students (though it houses some juniors and seniors as well). With spacious rooms, kitchens, and lounges, and within a close walking distance to H Mart, Riverside Park, and many restaurants outside campus, Carlton is a good way to get out of the Columbia bubble. ','A trek worth the view?','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/W2QZQ3K3DVCTZDYM2J75EDAY5A.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Large suites and rooms, plenty of space to chill with beautiful views#Spacious rooms and lounges ','Far from campus (~15 minute walk to campus)#No stairs to the basement (where the laundry room and bike storage is located)#Beware of the rats surrounding the building, especially on the nearby street ',40.803829,-73.968628,'placeholder','sophomores',1,'0',NULL),('East Campus','70 Morningside Drive','There\'s probably a party happening in East Campus tonight. Known as the rowdy senior dorm (though some juniors and a few sophomores live here as well), EC consists of townhouses, duplex suites, and two-person flats with private kitchens and bathrooms in each suite. Even though there\'s a party in this dorm at almost every hour, the walls are thicker than you might expect. Despite its infamous history of having moldy walls, most floors have been renovated since, and EC is one of the most popular senior housing options. You can enjoy a beautiful view overlooking downtown Manhattan while having a group living experience you will not regret. EC is also one of the few Columbia dorms with both air conditioning and a fitness room. ','Senior party central','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/EFNLDXHRUZGLXLXVPDGKLELKGU.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Large lounges, good for hosting parties#Rooms are nice with pretty views (especially for higher floors)#Fitness rooms on the eighth and 16th floors#Close to campus, the Faculty House and the Fac Shack ','Bathrooms and kitchens must be cleaned by residents#Townhouses have thinner walls (definitely not the quietest dorm)#Hard to get food delivered#Far from the 116th Street Columbia University subway station ',40.807102,-73.958916,'placeholder','juniors,seniors',2,'0',NULL),('Furnald Hall','Inside campus near Broadway and 115th Street','Housing first-years, this corridor-style dorm is the perfect place to live if you want a cozy environment to come home to after a busy day of classes. Furnald Hall is close to a lot of food options including Ferris Booth Commons, Pret a Manger, and Morton Williams. Each floor has spacious and clean lounges with kitchens, but no fridges, ideal for studying or watching movies with friends. The lobby area is also a popular hangout spot where you will find students working on homework throughout the day and late at night. Furnald Hall is the place to be if you want to live in a peaceful, clean setting with views overlooking the Columbia campus. ','A warm and cozy welcome','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/6JGJ344BQJDIZKMDDUEXHRYPT4.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Close to Lerner Hall and stores and restaurants on Broadway#Clean kitchens and lounge and very spacious bathrooms#Good storage space, shelves, and closets ','Sense of community can be hit-or-miss based on floor#A bit of a walk from other first-year hubs#Laundry rooms can be cramped#Walls are paper thin ',40.807415,-73.963882,'placeholder','first-years',0,'0',NULL),('Harmony Hall','544 West 110th Street','Harmony Hall is located on 110th Street between Amsterdam Avenue and Broadway and houses mostly juniors. It is a corridor-style residence hall with mostly singles, shared bathrooms, and a communal kitchen on every floor. It is rather secluded from main campus, but is closer to many Upper West Side restaurants and stores, offering an off-campus feel. It is a quiet dorm for those who enjoy having their peace of mind. Fun fact: Harmony Hall is also the name of a Vampire Weekend song, so if you are a fan of the band, consider looking into Harmony as one of your housing options. However, the band did confirm the song does not refer to this Harmony Hall. ','A step away from the hustle of campus','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/R4YHYMMJEFA2LJFVUZAIJODKLY.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Nice and cozy lounge on the first floor with a printer#The Cathedral Parkway 110th Street subway stop in front of H Mart is nearby ','The doorways are small, watch your head#The elevator is small, be prepared to squeeze#Far from main campus ',40.803657,-73.965857,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors',0,'0',NULL),('Hogan Hall','566 W. 114th Street','Hogan Hall, located on 114th Street between Broadway and Amsterdam Avenue, consists of spacious singles organized into suites. Each suite includes four, five, or six rooms along with a kitchen and private bathroom. With its close proximity to the Van Am Quad, Hogan is perfect for the senior who wants to spend their final year in Morningside Heights living the quintessential Columbia experience-equal part all-nighters in Butler and hosting wild ragers for friends.','A private space in a suite of friends','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/CUTGLXRG6RFGRILXFDBHMWE3EM.jpg',0,1,0,0,'Convenient location - close to John Jay, Butler, and Hamilton#Suite Style#Private kitchen and bathroom ','No A/C#No fitness room ',40.806332,-73.964561,'placeholder','seniors',2,'0',NULL),('River Hall','628 W. 114th St. (between Broadway and Riverside)','River Hall is located on 114th Street between Riverside Drive and Broadway. A senior dorm, it is made up of only singles, shared bathrooms, a common room, and a shared kitchen lounge on most floors. Its proximity to Riverside Park can be a plus for many, and it has both a music practice room and a fitness room in the basement. River Hall is relatively further down the hill on Riverside, so getting to campus can be a trek in the morning or the winter months, but if you are looking for somewhere quieter, you should definitely consider living here. ','Aptly Named','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/AVJRBOZL2RHUHMWEZFL4IBUJUE.jpg',0,1,0,0,'Close to campus#Kitchens have dishwashers#There are two or three kitchens per floor#It has a homey feel. It is quiet, but people are social and friendly#Home to Special Interest Communities ','The walls are thin#The rooms facing east or in the corner are shafted#There is only one elevator, which tends to move slowly#Slightly outdated building ',40.807362,-73.966362,'placeholder','seniors',0,'0',NULL),('Ruggles Hall','508 W. 114th Street','Ruggles Hall is located on 114th Street between Amsterdam Avenue and Broadway, right across from John Jay Hall. It consists of suites of four, six, or eight people, and houses mostly juniors, with some sophomores and seniors. The basement contains a spacious lounge with a small fitness center and a laundry room. Ruggles is a popular choice for upperclassmen who want to live with their friends and have quick access to main campus, dining halls such as JJ\'s Place, and local stores and services on Amsterdam Avenue. Located right on Frat Row, the noise level can definitely be a problem for some, but the community and convenience Ruggles offers make it a very solid choice. ','Social butterflies','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/OR7RADSPTFFMBGSNB455FHGKVQ.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Proximity to John Jay, main campus, and stores on Amsterdam Avenue#Suite-style with good single-use bathrooms#Variety of suite sizes to accommodate 4, 6, or 8-person housing groups#Good ambient heating ','Only one elevator for the whole floor#No AC#Stairs and hallways are narrow#Suite trash, kitchens, and bathrooms have to be cleaned by residents ',40.805752,-73.962692,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors',2,'0',NULL),('Schapiro Hall','605 W. 115th Street','Schapiro Hall is located on 115th Street between Broadway and Riverside Drive. It is a corridor-style dorm that houses sophomores, juniors, and seniors. The dorm is made up of singles as well as traditional and walk-through doubles. Floors two through nine have communal and single-use bathrooms, while floors 10 through 16 only have communal bathrooms. Each floor also has a kitchen without a fridge, connected to a lounge. It offers three speedy elevators, laundry in the basement, and a first-floor lounge, as well as less conventional features, like a mirrored dance room on the first floor and a sky lounge overlooking the Hudson River. ','So few cons','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/7O2CFNDANZGSXOHSL6H2O2UDPU.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Close to the Hooda Halal cart and Morton Williams, which is friendly for those midnight cravings#Dance room and individual piano practice rooms on the first floor#Well-furnished sky lounge with comfortable sofas and an excellent view that makes for a great study space#AC in every room ','Smaller room sizes#Lounges and kitchens are connected#Laundry room can be hot ',40.808495,-73.965302,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors',0,'0',NULL),('Watt Hall','549 W. 113th Street','Watt Hall is located on 113th Street between Amsterdam Avenue and Broadway, housing mostly juniors. It is made up of studio singles and doubles as well as one-bedroom and two-bedroom apartment-style rooms. There are private bathrooms and kitchens in each apartment, making Watt a favorite for those who want a more private, independent living experience, without being too removed from the main campus. Watt\'s proximity to Frat Row can be either a pro or a con depending on what kind of residential experience you are looking for.','Manhattan apartment vibes','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/RHHILY5NA5EJHIL6DQFLPBMSAQ.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Apartment style with private bathroom and kitchen#Convenient location; proximity to main campus and frats ','No A/C#Noise level ',40.806091,-73.96447,'placeholder','juniors,seniors',2,'0',NULL),('Woodbridge Hall','431 Riverside Drive','Woodbridge Hall is on Riverside Drive between 115th and 116th streets. The dorm houses mostly juniors and seniors and features apartment-style rooms that can be used either as walk-through doubles or regular doubles with a living room. In each one-bedroom apartment, there is also a private kitchen and bathroom. Woodbridge\'s vicinity to Riverside Park and relatively close location to campus are perfect for upperclassmen who want to feel more independent and have a real-world residential experience.','Home with a buddy','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/HZOJ4YFXDRHEPPLEWBJNV4ZGGA.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Apartment-style with private kitchen & bathroom#Large rooms#Gym on 1st floor ','No A/C#Distance from campus (on Riverside) ',40.808601,-73.966095,'placeholder','seniors',2,'0',NULL),('Hewitt Hall','The Quad (3009 Broadway)','Hewitt Hall is predominantly for first-years but is an option for upperclassmen who miss the convenience of living in the Quad. It is predominantly made up of singles, with a smattering of doubles and triples, and features communal bathrooms. Although you will need to be enrolled in, at minimum, Barnard\'s Flex 150 meal plan as an upperclassman in Hewitt, residents also have easy access to many restaurants on Broadway. By living in Hewitt, you are in close proximity to the 116th Street subway station, Hewitt Food Hall, and Barnard\'s campus; Hewitt is perfect for anyone who appreciates having their own privacy but still enjoys the lively atmosphere of living in the Quad. ','A space on the Quad','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/7ZVWYZFMFRFHXDLLL345DNGM7U.JPG',0,1,1,1,'On campus, close to 116th Street subway station and Hewitt Food Hall#Laundry on every floor#Computer lab in the basement ','Elevators are SLOW. Be prepared to take other Quad elevators#Lack of kitchens and upperclassmen must be enrolled in Barnard\'s Flex 150 meal plan, at minimum#Dorm is very old, a little musty, and the hallways look like they\'re from The Shining ',40.80878,-73.96411,'placeholder','first-years,sophomore,juniors',0,'0',NULL),('Elliott Hall','49 Claremont Avenue','Housing many singles and doubles, Elliot Hall may seem quiet and isolating, but if you look for it, you\'ll find a small but tight-knit community. Elliot is the perfect place for anyone looking for a calm living area where you can still get to know students around you. Elliot Hall is corridor-style, with two shared bathrooms and is close to Barnard (all you have to do is cross the street to get to the tunnels). Each floor has a cozy lounge and kitchen that is great for hanging out with friends or a chill study session. ','Finding community within a private space','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/MJEY3WTKGREW3AZP45BXXGKBYE.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Close proximity to campus#In the same building as Beyond Barnard#Opportunity to get a single ','Doubles can be on the smaller side#History of pests ',40.81025,-73.96388,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',1,'0',NULL),('Sulzberger Tower','The Quad (3009 Broadway)','Sulzberger Tower is located on the Barnard Quad and consists of single and double rooms from the ninth to the 17th floors of the Sulzberger building. Well known for its magnificent view overlooking the Hudson River and Morningside Heights, Sulzberger Tower is very popular among rising seniors, making it almost impossible for other students to get. It has a unique combination of the Quad\'s proximity to the dining halls and classrooms without the rowdiness and noise level that you might expect from the Quad.','Coveted views and location','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/PJM4UI6IVZDF3KTP2ZFCEGPMPM.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Location#Nice View#Quiet ','Shared floor bathroom and kitchens#Laundry only available on 8th floor ',40.808722,-73.963808,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',0,'0',NULL),('600 W 116th St.','600 West 116th Street','Just down the street from Shake Shack, 600 W. 116th St. has the prime location of being proximal to Riverside Park, Barnard\'s campus, and the west side of College Walk. In two- to seven-person suites, residents of 600 enjoy a shared kitchen, dining area, and bathroom. 600 is occupied by sophomores, juniors, and seniors who want to live in suites. Those who want to live in rooms with beautiful views and more space than most primarily sophomore or first-year housing should look to 600 as an option. ','Spacious rooms fit for a queen','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/CM7D2EHEZND3FGBCDIOVQKMUXI.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Second floor lounge has comfortable seating, a table, and a TV#Laundry on the second floor is very convenient ','Elevators are not always reliable#Potential pests#Mostly doubles unless you are a senior#Room size variability can be extreme ',40.80795,-73.96445,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',1,'0',NULL),('616 W 116th St.','616 W 116th St.','616 W. 116th St. boasts proximity to Barnard, Riverside Park, and Columbia\'s campus. With five- to six-person suites, residents of 616 W. 116th St. share a bathroom, kitchen, and dining area with fellow suitemates. Suites are largely composed of both singles and doubles, and a mix of upperclassmen live here. The building also has a computer lab and lounge space on the first floor. If you are a sophomore or older and want easy access to campus and amenities, check out 616 W. 116th St. ','A short skip to campus','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/W3YVQ22ELBC3DGNRZ3LEBCJU6E.jpg',0,1,1,0,'First-floor lounge is spacious and has a piano#Easy access to computers and printers in the computer lab ','Potential pests#Doubles can vary in size#Elevators are slow ',40.80827,-73.96523,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',1,'0',NULL),('620 W 116th St.','620 W 116th St.','Just a quick stroll from Barnard, 620 W. 116th St. is located conveniently close to Barnard\'s campus (with easy access to tunnels) and it lies on the corner right next to Riverside Park. 620 W. 116th St. offers a mix of four- to seven-person suites and has both singles and doubles. In each suite, students will get a shared dining area, shared kitchen, and bathroom. While it can be annoying to not have air conditioning in the first few months, if you\'re looking for a residence hall close to campus, look no further. ','Down the road from College Walk','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/S3O4XE2NQNBIPM3HMBRLRWTE7E.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Barnard residence hall closest to Riverside Park ','No AC#Potential rodents ',40.80838,-73.96548,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',1,'0',NULL),('601 W 110th St.','601 W 110th St.','If you want to leave dorms behind and feel like an adult, 601 West 110th Street may be for you. Located on 110th street, 110 boasts close proximity to many stores, like HMart and Westside Market, Riverside Park, the 1 train, and is only a few avenues away from Central Park West. Since 601 110 is a privately owned building, there is a mix of both students and tenants in the building. Suite range from 4 to 9 person suites and there are some single studio spaces offered. If you are looking for a dorm that allows you to separate your student identity from your home identity, and you don\'t mind walking a couple blocks to campus, maybe 110 is for you. ','For adulting','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/ZPQEXFLWVZFTRMZGXYFFEZJLAQ.jpg',0,1,1,1,'Most suites have living spaces#Good location with many stores nearby#Nice furniture (actual mattresses) ','Distance from campus#Not guaranteed AC ',40.80189,-73.96127,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',1,'0',NULL),('Cathedral Gardens','217 Manhattan Ave','Cathedral Gardens, located at the corner of 110th Street and Manhattan Avenue, is the farthest Barnard dorm from campus. Although the location may have its drawbacks, Cathedral Gardens is made up of some of the largest apartment-style suites Barnard housing offers. Each suite has its own private bathroom(s) as well as a kitchen and a lounge area. Cathedral Gardens houses mostly seniors and very lucky juniors and sophomores. Since it is secluded from the main campus, dining halls are pretty far, but there are still a variety of affordable restaurants and a grocery store close enough to make up for the distance.','A relaxing distance from college life','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/M536CBWKSRG5TBZZX7PUWGC6DE.jpg',0,1,1,0,'A/C#Spacious Suites#Private bathroom and kitchen ','Distance from Campus#One laundry room on 10th floor ',40.80081,-73.9601,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',1,'0',NULL),('Plimpton Hall','1235 Amsterdam Avenue','On the corner of 121st Street and Amsterdam Avenue, Plimpton Hall is the ideal dorm for students who want to be near campus but not caught up in the bustle. It contains apartment-style suites made up of four singles and a large double. Plimpton also includes its own lounge, computer lab, and laundry room and houses the Barnard Clay Studio. Although the dorm seems far, in reality, it is only a seven-minute walk from campus. Furthermore, it is conveniently located on top of a Dunkin\' and Appletree Market, a 24-hour grocery store and deli where you can buy late-night snacks or grab lunch. Plimpton allows you to discover another side of Morningside Heights and Harlem while still being in close proximity to campus.','Cozy suites with plentiful amenities','BARNARD','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/TLXZGID7WZFQFOT2QXJU6NZ3NQ.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Large rooms#Private bathroom and kitchen#A/C ','Distance to campus ',40.8097,-73.95854,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors,seniors',1,'0',NULL),('McBain Hall','562 West 113th Street','Located conveniently on the corner of 113th Street and Broadway, McBain Hall is one of the housing choices for sophomores at Columbia. McBain has mostly doubles with some singles in a corridor-style hall and has shared kitchens on most floors. Beware the shaft in the center of the building. While shafted rooms get little, if any, light, they do get air conditioning units, unlike the rest of the building. However, rooms that face east also get little to no light. If you currently enjoy living in Carman Hall, or if you are looking for a residence hall that knows how to have fun, McBain would be a great option for you to consider. You\'ll be close to many of your sophomore friends, and popular restaurants such as Community Food & Juice are barely a minute away. ','Sophomore Carman','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/U4MR5UO2A5BJXGOTMXL6ZA2RYI.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Fitness room on the fourth floor#Computer lab and study lounges on first floor#There are bathrooms and kitchens on each floor (except on the first floor) that are cleaned daily, Monday through Friday#Large doubles with great views if you\'re street facing and on a high floor#Laundry rooms have many machines and are clean ','No AC (but lounges and shafted rooms do!)#Two elevators, both of which are slow#May be noisy due to social atmosphere#Shaft doubles have no views and are fairly undesirable#Bad plumbing (shower temperature fluctuates) ',40.805931,-73.964951,'placeholder','sophomores',0,'0',NULL),('Wien Hall','411 W 116th St','Located on the eastern side of campus, Wien Hall is one of the housing options available to upperclassmen on Columbia\'s campus. Wien is corridor-style, made up of mostly singles and a few dozen doubles. Each floor has shared bathrooms with some floors having single-use bathrooms, and a lounge with a cooking area, but no fridge. Completed in 2018, the hall has undergone extensive renovations including new flooring, vanities, lounges, and radiators although air conditioning is still not available. Students enjoy Wien Hall mainly for its views of both Morningside Park and West Harlem on the top floors, the rooms\' personal sinks, and other features, including a piano and computer lounge. ','Over the bridge and through the gates. . . to Wien we go','COLUMBIA','https://arc-anglerfish-arc2-prod-spectator.s3.amazonaws.com/public/DT7CPFKRK5ASFERKEGIMYK5TVM.jpg',0,1,1,0,'Student Mail Center in the basement#Close to both Faculty House and Fac Shack#Sinks in the room!! ','Walls can be thin, can hear people in lounges#Can\'t control heater, rooms can get super dry, and no AC#Separated from other popular sophomore and junior dorms ',40.80665,-73.959803,'0 2 4 5 6 235','sophomores,juniors',0,'0',NULL),('Carman Hall','Inside campus on 114th Street and Broadway','One of Columbia\'s most iconic and popular first-year dorms, Carman Hall is the closest dorm on campus to Butler Library, Lerner Hall, and Frat Row. Composed entirely of doubles, all first-years in Carman will have a roommate, and it\'s known as the liveliest and most social of the freshmen dorms. Being so close to Frat Row, there\'s almost always a party nearby. There is never a temporary shortage of drinking water, snacks, or food since there is a drinking fountain on every floor and four vending machines. For more realmeals, Ferris Booth Commons is right next to Carman, and the various free-food events happening in Lerner are right around the corner. With a campus gate just steps away, you can add the 3 a.m. DoorDash employee to your social circle. While the dorm is infamous as the freshmen party dorm, it can also be the start of lasting friendships and a great dorm for someone looking to put themselves out there. ','Eat, party, and study','Columbia','https://theshaft.s3.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/carman/Carman+Hall/Annie_Son_The+Shaft_+Carman_29Nov21_CDS+-1.jpg',0,0,1,0,'One drinking water fountain per floor#Lively and social dorm#There is a classroom on the first floor, which doubles as a group study space at night ','No floor kitchens#Noise from frat parties ',40.8063,-73.9644,'','first-years',0,'0',NULL),('Wallach Hall','Inside campus near 115th Street','Located between Hartley Hall and John Jay Hall, Wallach Hall provides a balanced environment for first-year students looking for their own space while still being close to social hubs. Wallach is composed of mostly singles with some doubles in a (potentially confusing) semi-suite layout with single-use bathrooms and a full kitchen on each floor. With a cozy study lounge on the 10th floor and the gaming lounge on the first, all while being connected to John Jay Hall, Wallach is one of the most convenient dorms on campus. ','Convenience is key','Columbia','https://theshaft.s3.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/wallach/Wallach/Wallach-Yash+Mangalick-2.jpg',0,1,1,0,'The gaming lounge is right downstairs for those looking to grind out some games or just chill with friends#Connected by an accessible tunnel to John Jay Dining Hall, JJ\'s Place, and Hartley Hospitality Desk#Study lounge located on the 10th floor with a small library, good study spot ','Layout of hallways can be disorienting#Noise from Amsterdam Avenue can be very loud#Potential pest issues#Laundry in basement is shared with Hartley ',40.8061,-73.9619,'','first-years',0,'0',NULL),('Hartley Hall','Inside campus between 115th and 116th Streets','Like the name implies, Hartley Hall is a place full of heart, featuring cozy two-tiered suites with mostly singles and some doubles. A sophomore only dorm, Hartley additionally houses faculty-in-residence. The suites are each furnished with a kitchen on one level. The dorm also has a game room with pool and ping pong tables on the first floor, which is good for chilling with friends. Hartley\'s layout provides a sense of independence and community, all while being a short walk from John Jay Dining Hall, JJ\'s, and Butler Library. ','Close friends and close classes','Columbia','https://theshaft.s3.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/hartley/Hartley/KatSt.+Martin_Hartley_16.JPG',0,1,1,0,'Connected to John Jay Hall and Wallach Hall, a close walk to Butler Library and other parts of campus#Suite style is extremely cozy and gives good balance of social and private#In-suite kitchens are decently sized and well-furnished with good storage space#Hartley Hospitality Desk is in the dorm, so it is easy to get move-in/out bins and report maintenance issues, of which you\'ll probably have a few!#Some of the fastest elevators on campus ','Bathrooms can be a little crusty#Layout of the suites can be a little confusing#Laundry in basement is shared with Wallach#Potential pest problems, especially on lower floors ',40.8064,-73.9617,'','Sophomores',1,'0',NULL),('Brooks Hall','The Quad (3009 Broadway)','Located in the Quad, Brooks Hall is the oldest Barnard dorm. While corridor-style, Brooks dorms vary from dingles to quads. If you\'re lucky, you can score a dingle, or a double that is separated by a wall. While Brooks can be on the quieter side, you have easy access to the Sulzberger Hall lounge and all of Barnard\'s health amenities. Plus, Brooks showers are known to be spacious and envied by those all around the Quad. ','Room-sharing variety in the Quad','Barnard','https://theshaft.s3.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/brooks/10.jpg',0,1,1,1,'Built-in closets#Possibility to get a dingle#Spacious, typically clean showers ','Two showers per floor, potentially long wait times#Significant amount of quads#Shares an elevator with Reid Hall ',40.8084,-73.9643,'','first-years',0,'0',NULL),('Reid Hall','The Quad (3009 Broadway)','While there\'s no overall vibe to Reid Hall, there\'s still a strong sense of community among the residents. Made up entirely of doubles, Reid Hall\'s corridor-style layout makes it the perfect place to make new friends, such as your roommate or anyone else living on your floor. Not to mention, you can always hang out in a Sulzberger Hall lounge, as Reid residents have access to all the Quad\'s various amenities. ','Roommates to Friends Arc?','Barnard','https://theshaft.s3.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/reid/01.jpg',0,0,1,0,'Built-in closets#For Broadway-facing rooms, nice views of Columbia\'s entrance#There are water fountains on some floors ','Two showers per floor; depending on when you shower, be prepared to wait#Smaller room sizes on average#Share an RA with another dorm ',40.8083,-73.9641,'','first-years',0,'0',NULL),('Sulzberger Hall','The Quad (3009 Broadway)','Sulzberger Hall is the only first-year residence hall at Barnard that boasts air conditioning and is located in a prime spot. While predominantly made up of doubles, Sulzberger also houses a couple of triples. While Sulzberger is corridor-style and has communal bathrooms, there are typically two bathrooms per floor. Located right next to Sulzberger lounge and within close proximity to the rest of campus, Sulzberger is often highly coveted. ','Balance socializing and privacy','Barnard','https://theshaft.s3.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/sulzberger-hall/01.jpg',0,0,1,1,'Air conditioning#Easy access to the washer/dryers#For Broadway-facing rooms, nice views of the Columbia gates#Two bathrooms per floor ','No singles#Air conditioning gets turned off mid-first semester ',40.8087,-73.9639,'','first-years',0,'0',NULL),('John Jay Hall','Inside campus on 114th Street near Amsterdam Avenue','With convenient access to two dining halls and Columbia Health Medical Services within the building, John Jay Hall is a popular choice for first-year students. The rooms consist of mostly singles, with some walk-through and regular doubles. John Jay residents have their own private space but can also find a community with floor mates but with so many people, you probably won\'t meet everyone. Each floor has a lounge, but it\'s small and gatekept. Beware of the bathrooms. . . ','Late night JJ\'s run?','Columbia','https://theshaft.s3.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/john-jay/01.jpg',1,1,1,0,'John Jay Dining Hall, JJ\'s Place, and Columbia Health all in the building, so easy access#Access to Hartley Hall and Wallach Hall through the first floor#Rooms that face campus have nice views ','Bathrooms shared with the whole floor, can get messy#Smaller rooms on average#Elevators are slow. Be prepared to wait#15th floor doesn\'t have elevator access or a floor lounge ',40.8059,-73.9624,'','first-years',0,'0',NULL),('548 W 113th','548 West 113th Street','548 W 113th Street is located right on frat row so if you like hearing some music blasting through your windows, this would be the perfect dorm for you. Housing juniors and seniors, this brownstone is made up of all studio doubles, emulating a true New Yorker experience. With large kitchens and living rooms, your room could be the perfect hangout spot for your friends - and perhaps contribute to the frat row noise.\'','The true New Yorker experience','COLUMBIA','https://theshaft.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/548-w-113-st/01.jpg',0,0,1,0,'Private kitchen and bathroom#Good location#Spacious living areas\'','Possible late-night noise#No A/C#No elevator, walk-up only\'',40.80547,-73.96445,'placeholder','juniors,seniors',0,NULL,NULL),('611 W 112th','611 W 112th Street','Newly renovated bathrooms, rooms, and kitchens. What more could you possibly ask for? This is a corridor-style dorm consisting of mostly doubles with only seven singles. Consisting of three outdoor courtyards, you basically have a personal garden in NYC. 611 W. 112th has close access to campus, Westside, H-Mart, and non-dining hall food. Each room will have it’s own individual heating and cooling unit, which is great for unpredictable weather. This is the place to be if you want to be the first to sleep on brand new bed frames and mattresses!\'','The historic Maranamay hotel','COLUMBIA','https://theshaft.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/611-w-112-st/01.jpg',0,0,1,1,'Has A/C and heating#Brand new facilities#Outdoor courtyards#New outlet placement\'','Shafted rooms get no light#Distance from campus#New comes with mystery\'',40.80605,-73.9666,'placeholder','sophomores,juniors',0,NULL,NULL),('627 W 115th','627 West 115th Street','Who doesn\'t want the real New Yorker experience? This is a corridor-style brownstone that houses mostly rising juniors and seniors. Located on 115th street between Riverside and Broadway, you\'re close to campus, the 1 line, and everything you could possibly need. This dorm also houses Columbia\'s ONLY triple apartment, so if you want to live with two of your friends, this would be a great option. It\'s also a great way to get extra steps in because you will not have an elevator to use.\'','Columbia\'s hidden gem','COLUMBIA','https://theshaft.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/dorms/regulars/627-w-115-st/01.jpg',0,1,1,1,'Emulating the New Yorker life#Spacious apartments#The only 3-person suite#Quick access to campus\'','No elevator, walk-up only#No A/C\'',40.8088,-73.9652,'placeholder','juniors,seniors',0,NULL,NULL);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `dorm_static_info` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

